Z||000000||RobertVol||06-02-2000||07:31 PM||||I need to know the BEST place to get a AC compressor. The price I was qouted shocked me. Thought you guys could help. also opinions needed. Ignition coils....OEM ok OR is it worth to go with a top of the line aftermarket/ MSD, Jacobs, Accel which one and why/////???? <P>Thanks ||||reg||1
Z||000001||86se/lambo||06-02-2000||11:36 PM||||i replaced my compressor when doing my r-134 change, i got it at napa and paid $239, it has a life-time guartantee, as long as you buy the reciever drier with it. for me it was no fun taking it out... and i definately dont want to take it off again. remember to switch over the high side high pressure and high side low pressure switch ( if you have a v-5) or just the high pressure high side cut-off switch if you have the da6 model. i switched to the da6 because it's suppose to be a little beefier for the change in head pressure. anyway, i went for the accel coil and mounted it next to the dogbone.. and then redirected the auxillary fan tubes to blow in that direction.oh ya baby i got the hi rev thing going...now i just need a new prom and... and ...||||reg||10
Z||000002||RobertVol||06-02-2000||11:45 PM||||Tubes moved to it hmmmmm..cooler .good idea I never thought of that. But you like the accel coil? I hear opinions back in forth. Not worth it...but some feel it is worth it. Hey it may just "feel" faster but who cares ? feeling faster aint going faster but its better than "feeling slower" !   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I have also heard about Jacobs Coil being really good...anyone heard that ? ||||reg||14
